  "commit_message_example": "feat(auth): rotate refresh tokens and revoke the family on reuse\n\nRotationService.rotate issues a one-time token in the same family and marks the old one used in one\ntransaction; presenting a used token revokes the family. Expiry is compared with database time.\n\nSKM-Run: 0193a000-0000-7000-8000-000000000001\nSKM-Plan: 0192f5c4-0000-7000-8000-000000000c00\nSKM-Revision: 1\nSKM-Task: P1.2\nSKM-Attempt: 0193a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000a0012\nSKM-Output: 0193a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000e0002\nSKM-Review: 0193a000-0000-7000-8000-0000000f0002",
  "notes": [
    "Source: only the run stream of domain_events; seq is its stream_seq and the keyset cursor (execution.md §8). kind is a classification of the event type (StageStarted/StageCompleted -> stage, StageRecovered -> recovery).",
    "Skipped stages and diagnostics travel in the payload of StageStarted.skipped_stage_ids / StageCompleted.diagnostics; there is no separate source.",
    "AcceptanceDecided (seq 1030) is not terminal: TaskAccepted and TaskReady of dependents come only after integrate and the rerun_after_integration checks (K3).",
    "Control-plane stages (acceptance_gate here) are created and completed in one transaction, so they have no separate StageStarted entry.",
    "release_assignment emits no event; the worker's release after K5 is visible only as the assignment state."
  ]
}
